From 5cb806115970b218949d54a2b64fa89c26b8fc4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:26:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Contact shadows you notice, no band at the water's edge, a
 path of moonlight and froth round wading legs

Tuning from the first films of the contact shadows (#262) and the water
(#265), every changed number commented with why:

- The contact shadows' default is now what lookao 2 was, which read as a
  soft yard-wide shade along a step, under a barrel and in a wall's
  crease, with no rims or halos: the grade's per-hour strengths doubled
  (GAIN acts before the occlusion's clamp, so raising it is not the x2
  that was filmed). lookao stays relative to the new default.
- The water's mirror fades out over 22% of the screen toward its edge
  (was 6%) and the ripples break the hand-over to the sky up, so no
  straight, lighter band shows near the camera where mirrored rays leave
  the screen.
- The moon's path: the water's moon is the sky's (moon_dir_white, north-
  west, 24 to 55 degrees up from 23:00 to midnight); the first night film
  faced away from it. Its glint is broader and brighter (sharpness 160 to
  64, strength 1.2 to 2.0), a pale shimmer of small glints on the ripples.
- Froth round something standing in the water: a ring of six points on
  the surface finds the step the legs make in the bed behind it, and a
  lumpy froth spreads out from their outline, thinning over the ripples,
  where the shore's band drew a crisp, thin, bright oval (and a white
  ring round every reed base in the shallows). The shore's
  band is a little dimmer (0.75 to 0.6) and patchy with the ripples.

